  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 231 PM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nThrough next Thursday...\n\nDangerous heat will continue to worsen into the weekend. The \nstrong subtropical ridge (596-598DM) persists this afternoon \nacross the Gulf Coast region and remain in place through early \nnext week. This will lead to increasingly warm thermal profiles \nand strong subsidence across the Gulf Coast region. Rain chances \nwill remain squashed and shunted to the east-southeast (Pine Belt) \nthrough the weekend, with only limited coverage. The humidity has\ndropped some today with drier air aloft (GOES East PWs around 1.1\ninches in southwest half of the area). This has helped mixing to\nbe a little more efficient in some of those areas while further to\nthe north-northeast, heat concerns. Inherited heat graphics were\nmodified to single out the weekend into next week, where dangerous\nheat is more likely as the dry level air moves through/dissipates\nand less efficient mixing and higher heat stress will be a\nconcern. The worst timeframe is late weekend into early next week\n(Sunday-Monday), where heat indices could exceed 110F. Added a\nSignificant to the HWO graphics for the weekend into early next\nweek, with some of the outlooked area needing Extreme heat\nWarning headlines. The focus remains enough out in time to hold \noff introducing just yet. The ongoing heat headlines continue \nthrough the overnight periods with limited relief at night. Stay \ncool and hydrated and check on vulnerable populations and never \nleave children or pets unattended in hot vehicles as these can \nbecome lethal, as quickly as a matter of minutes.\n\nSome of the hottest days of the summer are expected, with highs\nlikely exceeding the century mark during the worst heat risk\nconcerns. Thermal profile climatology (21C to 25C at 850mb) \nindicate potential analogs into the low 100s (101F to 103F and \nmedian around 102F), with some higher values exceeding that. \nEven with that being said, some mixing could occur, which is\ntypical in this environment to support exceeding 100F degrees. \nRecord temperatures are likely during this timeframe into the\nweekend and early next week.\n\nRain and storm chances remain limited through the period, with\nonly peripheral areas in southeast MS seeing scarce showers and \nstorm coverage, mainly into early next week. Some relaxation of \nthe stout ridge will occur into early to mid next week. In \nconjunction with increased deeper moisture, increased convergence \nfrom frontal zone sagging southward may cause some better rain \ncoverage into early to mid next week. With dangerous heat, high \nhumidity and steep lapse rates, will have to monitor robust storm \npotential as this type of thermal setup is typically supportive of\nrobust diurnal microburst activity. Mostly dry conditions will \npersist most areas through the weekend, outside of the Pine Belt.\nAs the ridge gradually breaks down into mid week, storm coverage\nwill become scattered with highs and heat indices only a touch\nless oppressive. /DC/",
